Subject: [PATCH] roamd: let a Beam WRT router join as a node

Before a capture the controller checks the roamd release feed for a
package for the node's OpenWrt version and architecture. There is no
aarch64_cortex-a73 build there, so a Xiaomi BE7000 on Beam WRT was
reported as "repository unreachable" and could not be captured. Such a
node installs roamd from its own signed Beam WRT feed, which
mesh_node_install already falls back to, so treat it as ready.
---
diff --git a/package/roamd/src/mesh_discover.c b/package/roamd/src/mesh_discover.c
index fae7774..2d47d22 100644
--- a/package/roamd/src/mesh_discover.c
+++ b/package/roamd/src/mesh_discover.c
@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@ static const char *pkg_state(const char *os, const char *arch)
 	if (!os[0] || !arch[0])
 		return "missing";
 
+	/* Beam WRT (Xiaomi BE7000, the only aarch64_cortex-a73 build) has no
+	 * package in the roamd release feed: the node installs roamd from its
+	 * own signed feed, which mesh_node_install falls back to */
+	if (!strcmp(arch, "aarch64_cortex-a73"))
+		return "ready";
+
 	dot = strrchr(os, '.');
 	snprintf(branch, sizeof(branch), "%.*s",
 		 dot ? (int)(dot - os) : (int)strlen(os), os);
